        "date": "2026-11-13T20:57:27Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(setup): a post option changed on one setup never changes another's program\n\nWith two or more setups, an option edit (Skip pauses and homes, Output,\nThreading, End units) on a setup that follows the document's post\noptions now makes that setup's own options (SetSetupPostOptions,\nundoable) instead of writing the document's, which every other\nfollowing setup posts with. One setup keeps writing the document's\noptions as before. The setup's Post page says by name where an edit\nlands. Same law as #1515 (shared_mount_target).\n\nFixes #1526\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
